{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKd5SjExLf5stDoCoctVdH","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\tpolicy_version: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n     2\t\n     3\tservers:\n     4\t  hris:\n     5\t    endpoint: https://hris-mcp.hris.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n     6\t    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\n     7\t    downstream_audience: hris-mcp\n     8\t    owner: hris-platform\n     9\t  helpdesk:\n    10\t    endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    11\t    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\n    12\t    downstream_audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    13\t    owner: it-service-desk\n    14\t\n    15\t# Model-facing name -> qualified tool. Server annotations (readOnlyHint etc.)\n    16\t# are never consulted; approval comes only from this file.\n    17\ttools:\n    18\t  search_policies:\n    19\t    kind: local\n    20\t    reason: \"Answer policy questions from the approved HR handbook index.\"\n    21\t    scope: hr.policy.read\n    22\t    approval: none\n    23\t    input_schema:\n    24\t      type: object\n    25\t      properties:\n    26\t        query: {type: string, minLength: 3, maxLength: 300}\n    27\t      required: [query]\n    28\t      additionalProperties: false\n    29\t\n    30\t  get_leave_balance:\n    31\t    kind: mcp\n    32\t    qualified: hris/get_leave_balance\n    33\t    server: hris\n    34\t    reason: \"Show the asking employee their own leave balance.\"\n    35\t    scope: hris.leave.read\n    36\t    approval: none\n    37\t    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    38\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:5d1c0e9a7b3f48e2a61c9d04f7be3a92c815e6d07ab4f3c2e19d8a6b5c4f0e71\"\n    39\t    input_schema:\n    40\t      type: object\n    41\t      properties:\n    42\t        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n    43\t      required: [leave_type]\n    44\t      additionalProperties: false\n    45\t    output_schema:\n    46\t      type: object\n    47\t      properties:\n    48\t        leave_type: {type: string, maxLength: 20}\n    49\t        balance_days: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 400}\n    50\t        accrual_per_month: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 5}\n    51\t        as_of: {type: string, format: date}\n    52\t      required: [leave_type, balance_days, as_of]\n    53\t      additionalProperties: false\n    54\t\n    55\t  file_leave_request:\n    56\t    kind: mcp\n    57\t    qualified: hris/file_leave_request\n    58\t    server: hris\n    59\t    reason: \"File a leave request for the asking employee; the manager approves it in HRIS.\"\n    60\t    scope: hris.leave.request\n    61\t    approval: subject\n    62\t    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    63\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:a0f7c3d95e21b84f6c0d19e3a7b25f48d6e0c1a93b7f2e54d81c6a09f3e7b2d4\"\n    64\t    input_schema:\n    65\t      type: object\n    66\t      properties:\n    67\t        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n    68\t        start_date: {type: string, format: date}\n    69\t        end_date: {type: string, format: date}\n    70\t        note: {type: string, maxLength: 280}\n    71\t      required: [leave_type, start_date, end_date]\n    72\t      additionalProperties: false\n    73\t    output_schema:\n    74\t      type: object\n    75\t      properties:\n    76\t        request_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^LR-[0-9]{8}$\"}\n    77\t        status: {enum: [submitted, duplicate]}\n    78\t        approver_role: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n    79\t      required: [request_id, status]\n    80\t      additionalProperties: false\n    81\t\n    82\t  escalate_to_human:\n    83\t    kind: mcp\n    84\t    qualified: helpdesk/create_ticket\n    85\t    server: helpdesk\n    86\t    reason: \"Hand the conversation to an HR advisor when the agent cannot help.\"\n    87\t    scope: helpdesk.ticket.create\n    88\t    approval: subject\n    89\t    target: \"queue:hr-advisors\"\n    90\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:3e9b71f0c2d84a6e5b17f9c03d2a8e46b1f5c07d93a2e68b4c1d0f7a5e3b9c28\"\n    91\t    direct_route:\n    92\t      endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    93\t      audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    94\t    input_schema:\n    95\t      type: object\n    96\t      properties:\n    97\t        summary: {type: string, minLength: 10, maxLength: 1000}\n    98\t        category: {enum: [payroll, leave, benefits, conduct, other]}\n    99\t      required: [summary, category]\n   100\t      additionalProperties: false\n   101\t    output_schema:\n   102\t      type: object\n   103\t      properties:\n   104\t        ticket_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^HR-[0-9]{6}$\"}\n   105\t        queue: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n   106\t      required: [ticket_id]\n   107\t      additionalProperties: false\n     1\tapiVersion: v1\n     2\tkind: Namespace\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: hr-agent\n     5\t  labels:\n     6\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n     7\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.31\n     8\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n     9\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n    10\t    istio.io/dataplane-mode: ambient\n    11\t---\n    12\tapiVersion: kyverno.io/v1\n    13\tkind: ClusterPolicy\n    14\tmetadata:\n    15\t  name: hr-agent-verify-images\n    16\t  annotations:\n    17\t    policies.kyverno.io/owner: people-platform\n    18\tspec:\n    19\t  validationFailureAction: Enforce\n    20\t  failurePolicy: Fail\n    21\t  webhookTimeoutSeconds: 15\n    22\t  background: false\n    23\t  rules:\n    24\t    - name: only-approved-registry\n    25\t      match:\n    26\t        any:\n    27\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    28\t      validate:\n    29\t        message: \"Images in hr-agent must come from registry.acme.example and be referenced by digest.\"\n    30\t        pattern:\n    31\t          spec:\n    32\t            =(initContainers):\n    33\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    34\t            containers:\n    35\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    36\t    - name: verify-signature-and-provenance\n    37\t      match:\n    38\t        any:\n    39\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    40\t      verifyImages:\n    41\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent*\"]\n    42\t          mutateDigest: false\n    43\t          verifyDigest: true\n    44\t          required: true\n    45\t          attestors:\n    46\t            - entries:\n    47\t                - keyless:\n    48\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    49\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    50\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n    51\t          attestations:\n    52\t            - type: https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\n    53\t              attestors:\n    54\t                - entries:\n    55\t                    - keyless:\n    56\t                        subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    57\t                        issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    58\t              conditions:\n    59\t                - all:\n    60\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.buildType }}\"\n    61\t                      operator: Equals\n    62\t                      value: \"https://actions.github.io/buildtypes/workflow/v1\"\n    63\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.repository }}\"\n    64\t                      operator: Equals\n    65\t                      value: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent\"\n    66\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.ref }}\"\n    67\t                      operator: Equals\n    68\t                      value: \"refs/heads/main\"\n    69\t                    - key: \"{{ runDetails.builder.id }}\"\n    70\t                      operator: Equals\n    71\t                      value: \"https://github.com/actions/runner/github-hosted\"\n    72\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/platform/*\"]\n    73\t          mutateDigest: false\n    74\t          verifyDigest: true\n    75\t          required: true\n    76\t          attestors:\n    77\t            - entries:\n    78\t                - keyless:\n    79\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/platform-images/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    80\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    81\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"mcpServers\": {\n     3\t    \"hr-tool-gateway\": {\n     4\t      \"type\": \"http\",\n     5\t      \"url\": \"https://hr-tool-gateway.hr-agent.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\",\n     6\t      \"headers\": {\n     7\t        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${HR_GATEWAY_TOKEN}\"\n     8\t      }\n     9\t    }\n    10\t  }\n    11\t}\n\"\"\"Tool registry: the only tools this agent can see or call.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pathlib\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport yaml\n\nCONFIG_DIR = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"config\"\n\n\ndef load_yaml(name: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    with open(CONFIG_DIR / name, encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        return yaml.safe_load(fh)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ToolSpec:\n    name: str\n    kind: str\n    qualified: str\n    reason: str\n    scope: str\n    approval: str\n    input_schema: dict[str, Any]\n    output_schema: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    server: str | None = None\n    target_template: str | None = None\n    fingerprint: str | None = None\n    direct_route: dict[str, str] | None = field(default=None, hash=False)\n\n    def target(self, subject: str) -> str:\n        return (self.target_template or self.qualified).format(subject=subject)\n\n\nclass ToolRegistry:\n    def __init__(self, raw: dict[str, Any]):\n        self.policy_version: str = raw[\"policy_version\"]\n        self.servers: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = raw[\"servers\"]\n        self._tools: dict[str, ToolSpec] = {}\n        for name, t in raw[\"tools\"].items():\n            if not t.get(\"reason\"):\n                raise ValueError(f\"tool {name} has no task reason\")\n            if t[\"approval\"] not in (\"none\", \"subject\"):\n                raise ValueError(f\"tool {name}: unknown approval mode\")\n            self._tools[name] = ToolSpec(\n                name=name,\n                kind=t[\"kind\"],\n                qualified=t.get(\"qualified\", name),\n                reason=t[\"reason\"],\n                scope=t[\"scope\"],\n                approval=t[\"approval\"],\n                input_schema=t[\"input_schema\"],\n                output_schema=t.get(\"output_schema\"),\n                server=t.get(\"server\"),\n                target_template=t.get(\"target\"),\n                fingerprint=t.get(\"fingerprint\"),\n                direct_route=t.get(\"direct_route\"),\n            )\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_config(cls) -> \"ToolRegistry\":\n        return cls(load_yaml(\"tools.yaml\"))\n\n    def get(self, name: str) -> ToolSpec | None:\n        # Exact key lookup only; no prefix, case folding or alias matching.\n        return self._tools.get(name)\n\n    def by_qualified(self, qualified: str) -> ToolSpec | None:\n        for spec in self._tools.values():\n            if spec.qualified == qualified:\n                return spec\n        return None\n\n    def model_schemas(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        return [\n            {\"name\": s.name, \"description\": s.reason, \"input_schema\": s.input_schema}\n            for s in self._tools.values()\n        ]\n# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n\n## Components\n\n| Component | Code | Identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n\n## How a request flows\n\n1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n\nEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n```\n\nRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\ncalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\nLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n\n## Audit retention\n\nAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\nPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n`hr_audit_reader`.\n\n## Releases\n\nMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\nrecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\ndiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\nworkflow from `main`.\n<class 'dict'> ['A01', 'A02', 'A03', 'A04', 'A05']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71f043ed-19c9-490b-9dd2-a2aeb708a377","uuid":"a676120d-2d9b-40c1-9552-0040318f7780","timestamp":"2026-11-21T12:01:13.640Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\tpolicy_version: \"2026-09-18.3\"\n     2\t\n     3\tservers:\n     4\t  hris:\n     5\t    endpoint: https://hris-mcp.hris.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n     6\t    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp\n     7\t    downstream_audience: hris-mcp\n     8\t    owner: hris-platform\n     9\t  helpdesk:\n    10\t    endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    11\t    identity: spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp\n    12\t    downstream_audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    13\t    owner: it-service-desk\n    14\t\n    15\t# Model-facing name -> qualified tool. Server annotations (readOnlyHint etc.)\n    16\t# are never consulted; approval comes only from this file.\n    17\ttools:\n    18\t  search_policies:\n    19\t    kind: local\n    20\t    reason: \"Answer policy questions from the approved HR handbook index.\"\n    21\t    scope: hr.policy.read\n    22\t    approval: none\n    23\t    input_schema:\n    24\t      type: object\n    25\t      properties:\n    26\t        query: {type: string, minLength: 3, maxLength: 300}\n    27\t      required: [query]\n    28\t      additionalProperties: false\n    29\t\n    30\t  get_leave_balance:\n    31\t    kind: mcp\n    32\t    qualified: hris/get_leave_balance\n    33\t    server: hris\n    34\t    reason: \"Show the asking employee their own leave balance.\"\n    35\t    scope: hris.leave.read\n    36\t    approval: none\n    37\t    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    38\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:5d1c0e9a7b3f48e2a61c9d04f7be3a92c815e6d07ab4f3c2e19d8a6b5c4f0e71\"\n    39\t    input_schema:\n    40\t      type: object\n    41\t      properties:\n    42\t        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n    43\t      required: [leave_type]\n    44\t      additionalProperties: false\n    45\t    output_schema:\n    46\t      type: object\n    47\t      properties:\n    48\t        leave_type: {type: string, maxLength: 20}\n    49\t        balance_days: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 400}\n    50\t        accrual_per_month: {type: number, minimum: 0, maximum: 5}\n    51\t        as_of: {type: string, format: date}\n    52\t      required: [leave_type, balance_days, as_of]\n    53\t      additionalProperties: false\n    54\t\n    55\t  file_leave_request:\n    56\t    kind: mcp\n    57\t    qualified: hris/file_leave_request\n    58\t    server: hris\n    59\t    reason: \"File a leave request for the asking employee; the manager approves it in HRIS.\"\n    60\t    scope: hris.leave.request\n    61\t    approval: subject\n    62\t    target: \"employee:{subject}\"\n    63\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:a0f7c3d95e21b84f6c0d19e3a7b25f48d6e0c1a93b7f2e54d81c6a09f3e7b2d4\"\n    64\t    input_schema:\n    65\t      type: object\n    66\t      properties:\n    67\t        leave_type: {enum: [annual, sick, parental, unpaid]}\n    68\t        start_date: {type: string, format: date}\n    69\t        end_date: {type: string, format: date}\n    70\t        note: {type: string, maxLength: 280}\n    71\t      required: [leave_type, start_date, end_date]\n    72\t      additionalProperties: false\n    73\t    output_schema:\n    74\t      type: object\n    75\t      properties:\n    76\t        request_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^LR-[0-9]{8}$\"}\n    77\t        status: {enum: [submitted, duplicate]}\n    78\t        approver_role: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n    79\t      required: [request_id, status]\n    80\t      additionalProperties: false\n    81\t\n    82\t  escalate_to_human:\n    83\t    kind: mcp\n    84\t    qualified: helpdesk/create_ticket\n    85\t    server: helpdesk\n    86\t    reason: \"Hand the conversation to an HR advisor when the agent cannot help.\"\n    87\t    scope: helpdesk.ticket.create\n    88\t    approval: subject\n    89\t    target: \"queue:hr-advisors\"\n    90\t    fingerprint: \"sha256:3e9b71f0c2d84a6e5b17f9c03d2a8e46b1f5c07d93a2e68b4c1d0f7a5e3b9c28\"\n    91\t    direct_route:\n    92\t      endpoint: https://helpdesk-mcp.helpdesk.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\n    93\t      audience: helpdesk-mcp\n    94\t    input_schema:\n    95\t      type: object\n    96\t      properties:\n    97\t        summary: {type: string, minLength: 10, maxLength: 1000}\n    98\t        category: {enum: [payroll, leave, benefits, conduct, other]}\n    99\t      required: [summary, category]\n   100\t      additionalProperties: false\n   101\t    output_schema:\n   102\t      type: object\n   103\t      properties:\n   104\t        ticket_id: {type: string, pattern: \"^HR-[0-9]{6}$\"}\n   105\t        queue: {type: string, maxLength: 40}\n   106\t      required: [ticket_id]\n   107\t      additionalProperties: false\n     1\tapiVersion: v1\n     2\tkind: Namespace\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: hr-agent\n     5\t  labels:\n     6\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n     7\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.31\n     8\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n     9\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n    10\t    istio.io/dataplane-mode: ambient\n    11\t---\n    12\tapiVersion: kyverno.io/v1\n    13\tkind: ClusterPolicy\n    14\tmetadata:\n    15\t  name: hr-agent-verify-images\n    16\t  annotations:\n    17\t    policies.kyverno.io/owner: people-platform\n    18\tspec:\n    19\t  validationFailureAction: Enforce\n    20\t  failurePolicy: Fail\n    21\t  webhookTimeoutSeconds: 15\n    22\t  background: false\n    23\t  rules:\n    24\t    - name: only-approved-registry\n    25\t      match:\n    26\t        any:\n    27\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    28\t      validate:\n    29\t        message: \"Images in hr-agent must come from registry.acme.example and be referenced by digest.\"\n    30\t        pattern:\n    31\t          spec:\n    32\t            =(initContainers):\n    33\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    34\t            containers:\n    35\t              - image: \"registry.acme.example/*@sha256:*\"\n    36\t    - name: verify-signature-and-provenance\n    37\t      match:\n    38\t        any:\n    39\t          - resources: {kinds: [Pod], namespaces: [hr-agent]}\n    40\t      verifyImages:\n    41\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/people/hr-helpdesk-agent*\"]\n    42\t          mutateDigest: false\n    43\t          verifyDigest: true\n    44\t          required: true\n    45\t          attestors:\n    46\t            - entries:\n    47\t                - keyless:\n    48\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    49\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    50\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n    51\t          attestations:\n    52\t            - type: https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\n    53\t              attestors:\n    54\t                - entries:\n    55\t                    - keyless:\n    56\t                        subject: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent/.github/workflows/release.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    57\t                        issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    58\t              conditions:\n    59\t                - all:\n    60\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.buildType }}\"\n    61\t                      operator: Equals\n    62\t                      value: \"https://actions.github.io/buildtypes/workflow/v1\"\n    63\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.repository }}\"\n    64\t                      operator: Equals\n    65\t                      value: \"https://github.com/acme/hr-helpdesk-agent\"\n    66\t                    - key: \"{{ buildDefinition.externalParameters.workflow.ref }}\"\n    67\t                      operator: Equals\n    68\t                      value: \"refs/heads/main\"\n    69\t                    - key: \"{{ runDetails.builder.id }}\"\n    70\t                      operator: Equals\n    71\t                      value: \"https://github.com/actions/runner/github-hosted\"\n    72\t        - imageReferences: [\"registry.acme.example/platform/*\"]\n    73\t          mutateDigest: false\n    74\t          verifyDigest: true\n    75\t          required: true\n    76\t          attestors:\n    77\t            - entries:\n    78\t                - keyless:\n    79\t                    subject: \"https://github.com/acme/platform-images/.github/workflows/build.yml@refs/heads/main\"\n    80\t                    issuer: \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\"\n    81\t                    rekor: {url: \"https://rekor.sigstore.dev\"}\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"mcpServers\": {\n     3\t    \"hr-tool-gateway\": {\n     4\t      \"type\": \"http\",\n     5\t      \"url\": \"https://hr-tool-gateway.hr-agent.svc.cluster.local:8443/mcp\",\n     6\t      \"headers\": {\n     7\t        \"Authorization\": \"Bearer ${HR_GATEWAY_TOKEN}\"\n     8\t      }\n     9\t    }\n    10\t  }\n    11\t}\n\"\"\"Tool registry: the only tools this agent can see or call.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pathlib\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport yaml\n\nCONFIG_DIR = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"config\"\n\n\ndef load_yaml(name: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    with open(CONFIG_DIR / name, encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        return yaml.safe_load(fh)\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ToolSpec:\n    name: str\n    kind: str\n    qualified: str\n    reason: str\n    scope: str\n    approval: str\n    input_schema: dict[str, Any]\n    output_schema: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    server: str | None = None\n    target_template: str | None = None\n    fingerprint: str | None = None\n    direct_route: dict[str, str] | None = field(default=None, hash=False)\n\n    def target(self, subject: str) -> str:\n        return (self.target_template or self.qualified).format(subject=subject)\n\n\nclass ToolRegistry:\n    def __init__(self, raw: dict[str, Any]):\n        self.policy_version: str = raw[\"policy_version\"]\n        self.servers: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = raw[\"servers\"]\n        self._tools: dict[str, ToolSpec] = {}\n        for name, t in raw[\"tools\"].items():\n            if not t.get(\"reason\"):\n                raise ValueError(f\"tool {name} has no task reason\")\n            if t[\"approval\"] not in (\"none\", \"subject\"):\n                raise ValueError(f\"tool {name}: unknown approval mode\")\n            self._tools[name] = ToolSpec(\n                name=name,\n                kind=t[\"kind\"],\n                qualified=t.get(\"qualified\", name),\n                reason=t[\"reason\"],\n                scope=t[\"scope\"],\n                approval=t[\"approval\"],\n                input_schema=t[\"input_schema\"],\n                output_schema=t.get(\"output_schema\"),\n                server=t.get(\"server\"),\n                target_template=t.get(\"target\"),\n                fingerprint=t.get(\"fingerprint\"),\n                direct_route=t.get(\"direct_route\"),\n            )\n\n    @classmethod\n    def from_config(cls) -> \"ToolRegistry\":\n        return cls(load_yaml(\"tools.yaml\"))\n\n    def get(self, name: str) -> ToolSpec | None:\n        # Exact key lookup only; no prefix, case folding or alias matching.\n        return self._tools.get(name)\n\n    def by_qualified(self, qualified: str) -> ToolSpec | None:\n        for spec in self._tools.values():\n            if spec.qualified == qualified:\n                return spec\n        return None\n\n    def model_schemas(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n        return [\n            {\"name\": s.name, \"description\": s.reason, \"input_schema\": s.input_schema}\n            for s in self._tools.values()\n        ]\n# hr-helpdesk-agent\n\nAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\nshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\nthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n\n## Components\n\n| Component | Code | Identity |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n\n## How a request flows\n\n1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n\nEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n\n## Stopping the agent\n\nOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n\n```sql\nINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n```\n\nRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\ncalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\nLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n\n## Audit retention\n\nAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\nPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n`hr_audit_reader`.\n\n## Releases\n\nMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\nrecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\ndiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\nworkflow from `main`.\n<class 'dict'> ['A01', 'A02', 'A03', 'A04', 'A05']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BKd5SjExLf5stDoCoctVdH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
