{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVGt9zDY8fhGJUjVUfzFYt","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.10\n     2\tFROM python:3.12.7-slim-bookworm@sha256:032c52613401895aa3d418a4c5bf5c3ad0d5d6fe3c1e9b2c8b5d0a7e6f4c3b21 AS build\n     3\tENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1\n     4\tWORKDIR /build\n     5\tCOPY requirements.txt .\n     6\tRUN pip install --require-hashes --only-binary=:all: --target /deps -r requirements.txt\n     7\t\n     8\tFROM gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian12:nonroot@sha256:7e4c1d2a9f3b8e60c5d47a19b2f03e8d6c1a5b94f7e2d03c8a6b1f5e9d4c2a70\n     9\tENV PYTHONPATH=/deps:/app PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1\n    10\tWORKDIR /app\n    11\tCOPY --from=build /deps /deps\n    12\tCOPY --chown=0:0 requirements.txt Dockerfile ./\n    13\tCOPY --chown=0:0 src/ src/\n    14\tCOPY --chown=0:0 prompts/ prompts/\n    15\tCOPY --chown=0:0 config/ config/\n    16\tUSER 65532:65532\n    17\tENTRYPOINT [\"python3\"]\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}]\n                 [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER]\n                 [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}]\n                 [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY]\n                 [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS]\n                 [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM]\n                 [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\npositional arguments:\n  findings\n  {check,flag,item,prescan,next}\n  target\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --repo REPO\n  --met {yes,no,unknown}\n  --evidence EVIDENCE\n  --quote QUOTE\n  --counter COUNTER\n  --note NOTE\n  --rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}\n  --confidence {high,medium,low}\n  --summary SUMMARY\n  --next NEXT_STEP\n  --violates VIOLATES\n  --also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS\n  --verdict {confirmed,dismissed}\n  --item ITEM\n  --reason REASON\nusage: review_coverage.py [-h] {inventory,policy,ledger} ...\n\nStatic candidate inventory and evidence ledger. Never executes repository code.\n\npython review_coverage.py inventory REPO\npython review_coverage.py ledger FINDINGS.json CHECK --rows rows.json --attempts attempts.json\n\nInventory matches are candidates, not findings or proof of completeness. Review\naliases, wrappers, computed calls and unsupported languages manually as well.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {inventory,policy,ledger}\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71f043ed-19c9-490b-9dd2-a2aeb708a377","uuid":"6b306a83